From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Poul Sander <poul@poulsander.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:51:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] OpenArena: cgame syscalls 112/113 (LFX particles, view
 position)

The OpenArena engine uses cgame syscall 112 for trap_R_LFX_ParticleEffect
and 113 for trap_R_GetViewPosition. Quake3e used 112 for
CG_R_ADDREFENTITYTOSCENE2, so an OpenArena cgame calling the particle
trap dropped with "RE_AddRefEntityToScene: bad reType". Reserve the
OpenArena numbers (particles are a no-op, view position reports off
screen) and move the Quake3e extensions to 120+. Quake3e mods find them
through trap_GetValue, so the renumbering does not affect them.
---
 code/cgame/cg_public.h |  9 +++++++--
 code/client/cl_cgame.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/code/cgame/cg_public.h b/code/cgame/cg_public.h
index c92bf000..098072f1 100644
--- a/code/cgame/cg_public.h
+++ b/code/cgame/cg_public.h
@@ -177,8 +177,13 @@ typedef enum {
 	CG_TESTPRINTFLOAT,
 	CG_ACOS,
 
-	// engine extensions
-	CG_R_ADDREFENTITYTOSCENE2,
+	// OpenArena engine extensions, same numbers as engine-openarena so that
+	// OpenArena cgame builds keep working (accepted, but not implemented)
+	CG_R_LFX_PARTICLEEFFECT = 112,
+	CG_R_VIEWPOSITION,
+
+	// engine extensions, discovered via trap_GetValue so the numbers may move
+	CG_R_ADDREFENTITYTOSCENE2 = 120,
 	CG_R_FORCEFIXEDDLIGHTS,
 	CG_R_ADDLINEARLIGHTTOSCENE,
 	CG_IS_RECORDING_DEMO,
diff --git a/code/client/cl_cgame.c b/code/client/cl_cgame.c
index 4379da01..b3a5c563 100644
--- a/code/client/cl_cgame.c
+++ b/code/client/cl_cgame.c
@@ -787,6 +787,18 @@ static intptr_t CL_CgameSystemCalls( intptr_t *args ) {
 	case CG_R_INPVS:
 		return re.inPVS( VMA(1), VMA(2) );
 
+	// OpenArena engine extensions
+	case CG_R_LFX_PARTICLEEFFECT:
+		// renderer particle system of the OpenArena engine, not available here
+		return 0;
+
+	case CG_R_VIEWPOSITION:
+		// OpenArena projects the point to window coordinates and writes
+		// -666,-666 when it is off screen; we have no view matrices here
+		((float *)VMA(1))[0] = -666.0f;
+		((float *)VMA(1))[1] = -666.0f;
+		return 0;
+
 	// engine extensions
 	case CG_R_ADDREFENTITYTOSCENE2:
 		re.AddRefEntityToScene( VMA(1), qtrue );
-- 
2.53.0

